{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>that one hunts game of a wild animal.</b> Such as deer and gazelle." "<b>or bird that may be eaten.</b> From this verse too we learn that we may not let the stranger eat in our land pig or horse or bird of prey, which is unclean. And it is possible that because He commanded not to eat blood and not to see blood poured out apart from the altar, HaShem commanded to cover all blood that is not offered upon the altar — so that the one who sees it, upon seeing it, and it is blood of a deer or gazelle or bird, will not suppose that a sacrifice was slaughtered for idolatry. And in the section Re'eh I shall explain the secret of this verse."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:34.083861547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}